WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.674
[opening theme music playing]

01:46.731 --> 01:47.941
[music fades]

01:49.526 --> 01:56.533
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

02:01.454 --> 02:06.126
1 YEAR AGO
ONGSEONG HOSPITAL, GYEONGSEONG

02:10.922 --> 02:15.093
Ah, Sachimoto Ryu,
Tokyo University of the Arts.

02:15.969 --> 02:17.095
You applied on your own?

02:17.178 --> 02:18.179
Uh, yes.

02:18.680 --> 02:21.766
I wanted to serve.
I wanted to serve the Empire of Japan.

02:21.850 --> 02:24.477
Well, the pay is not too bad either, huh?

02:25.478 --> 02:26.312
[chuckles]

02:33.361 --> 02:34.988
What is this book for, sir?

02:35.572 --> 02:37.240
The New Text on Anatomy.

02:38.116 --> 02:40.785
Oh, I haven't seen this one yet.

02:41.953 --> 02:46.249
[man 1] Books like these have been around
in Germany since 1722.

02:46.749 --> 02:49.169
Though our own empire is lagging behind,

02:49.252 --> 02:51.921
we are striving to elevate
our medical standards for the future

02:52.005 --> 02:53.756
here at Ongseong Hospital

02:53.840 --> 02:55.300
through study and research,

02:55.383 --> 02:57.510
and, of course, future experiments.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.889
Your job is to record
everything we do here. Understood?

03:01.681 --> 03:04.100
So you want… me to

03:04.184 --> 03:05.643
draw what exactly, sir?

03:05.727 --> 03:07.979
- [dramatic music playing]
- [pained moaning]

03:11.524 --> 03:14.694
Now, which part shall we work on today?

03:16.696 --> 03:18.990
Since we have a new artist with us,

03:19.073 --> 03:20.658
let's begin with the abdomen.

03:21.159 --> 03:23.328
- Let's cut the middle.
- [man 2] Yes, sir.

03:23.411 --> 03:24.621
[groaning]

03:24.704 --> 03:25.538
[man 1] Scalpel.

03:27.040 --> 03:28.291
Doctor, I don't wanna die!

03:28.374 --> 03:31.002
Please don't kill me!
Please, Doctor, let me live!

03:31.085 --> 03:32.212
Oh, please!

03:32.295 --> 03:35.131
Please don't do this!
Please don't kill me! Cu--

03:35.215 --> 03:36.966
[screaming]

03:40.220 --> 03:42.013
[groaning]

03:43.056 --> 03:44.474
[Sachimoto panting]

03:44.557 --> 03:45.516
[gagging]

03:47.810 --> 03:48.686
[retching]

03:48.770 --> 03:49.938
[man 1] Sachimoto?

03:50.021 --> 03:51.105
Sachimoto!

03:51.856 --> 03:53.566
Get back in here right now!

03:53.650 --> 03:57.612
[Sachimoto] I was merely a starving artist
struggling to survive.

03:57.695 --> 03:59.030
[coughs, breathes heavily]

03:59.113 --> 04:00.240
I needed money,

04:01.074 --> 04:03.868
so I chose Joseon
after hearing about the high pay.

04:03.952 --> 04:04.911
But…

04:04.994 --> 04:05.912
[grunts]

04:11.042 --> 04:13.044
[inhales shakily, exhales sharply]

04:13.127 --> 04:15.171
[solemn instrumental music playing]

04:18.675 --> 04:20.051
[Sachimoto sobbing gently]

04:21.803 --> 04:22.720
[door closes]

04:27.308 --> 04:28.643
[woman] No need to cry.

04:31.771 --> 04:33.314
You'll get used to it soon enough.

04:33.398 --> 04:35.858
You'll grow numb to it,
just like everyone else here.

04:37.694 --> 04:39.320
That seems to be human nature.

04:39.904 --> 04:43.825
It seems we all have the ability…
to adapt pretty quickly to anything.

04:45.076 --> 04:46.703
Whether it's horrible pain…

04:49.872 --> 04:51.457
or disillusionment.

04:54.669 --> 04:55.503
[door opens]

04:55.586 --> 04:58.047
Hey, you. Time's up. Hurry up.

04:58.131 --> 04:59.632
[footsteps receding]

05:05.263 --> 05:06.264
[door closes]

05:06.347 --> 05:07.181
[sniffles]

05:08.474 --> 05:09.976
[suspenseful music playing]

05:13.896 --> 05:14.897
[distant coughing]

05:16.190 --> 05:18.484
[doors unlocking, locking]

05:19.610 --> 05:20.820
[distant coughing]

05:24.115 --> 05:25.450
[distant coughing]

05:26.576 --> 05:27.994
[distant whimpering]

05:32.332 --> 05:33.666
[melancholy music playing]

05:54.687 --> 05:55.563
[grunts softly]

05:57.732 --> 05:59.525
[grunting, gasping]

05:59.609 --> 06:00.568
[breathing rapidly]

06:00.651 --> 06:01.569
[squelching]

06:02.153 --> 06:03.696
[ominous music playing]

06:04.197 --> 06:05.406
[squelching]

06:05.490 --> 06:06.991
[grunting]

06:10.870 --> 06:12.372
[panting]

06:18.669 --> 06:20.421
[screeching]

06:20.505 --> 06:22.673
- [dramatic music playing]
- [door clanging]

06:25.843 --> 06:27.095
[door rattling]

06:28.971 --> 06:29.889
[snarling]

06:31.307 --> 06:32.725
[screeching]

06:39.732 --> 06:41.109
[breathing heavily]

06:42.693 --> 06:44.112
- [music fades]
- [groans]

06:44.195 --> 06:45.571
[unsettling music playing]

06:46.072 --> 06:47.990
[breathing shakily]

06:58.000 --> 06:59.710
[creature breathing heavily]

07:16.519 --> 07:20.022
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN LONGING AND ANGUISH

07:20.106 --> 07:22.483
EPISODE 2
MOTHER

07:30.908 --> 07:32.410
[wistful music playing]

07:48.885 --> 07:51.262
[Chae-ok] Why did you ever agree
to work with him?

07:51.846 --> 07:54.390
There wasn't a particular reason
to turn him down

07:54.474 --> 07:58.728
We'll help him find the missing girl,
and he will get information on Sachimoto.

07:59.312 --> 08:01.772
- But the man's selfish and shameless.
- [chuckles]

08:02.315 --> 08:04.317
Don't be so quick to judge Master Jang.

08:05.234 --> 08:06.944
The way he speaks is so crude,

08:08.321 --> 08:10.907
and he brushes off
other people's issues so lightly.

08:10.990 --> 08:14.535
Chae-ok, you have to understand
we're just a couple of sleuths to him.

08:16.829 --> 08:18.372
We've already agreed,

08:18.456 --> 08:20.666
so now we'll just focus on
benefitting each other.

08:23.044 --> 08:24.086
I'm not sure.

08:26.047 --> 08:27.632
I've got a bad feeling about this.

08:29.550 --> 08:32.136
Like when we were
on Manwol Island, I had a hunch,

08:33.429 --> 08:35.765
then you were injured,
and it turned out I was right.

08:38.684 --> 08:41.145
This will be our final case together,
got that?

08:43.773 --> 08:47.527
After we find the missing girl,
I think you should go home, all right?

08:48.152 --> 08:49.362
What about Mother, then?

08:51.614 --> 08:52.448
From now on,

08:52.532 --> 08:54.909
the burden of finding your mother
is mine alone to bear.

08:56.327 --> 08:59.288
She wouldn't have wanted
this life for you. You need to stop.

08:59.372 --> 09:02.250
- Father, listen--
- [father] You should live your own life.

09:04.460 --> 09:06.462
This is where the road ends for us.

09:16.597 --> 09:17.473
[sighs]

09:29.277 --> 09:30.695
[Tae-sang] Till the cherry blossoms

09:31.445 --> 09:32.613
lose their flowers.

09:34.073 --> 09:35.992
[gentle music playing]

09:49.964 --> 09:51.090
[music fades]

09:52.049 --> 09:55.261
So, what did you think…
about these sleuths we talked to?

09:56.262 --> 09:58.014
Think they'll be able to find Myeong-ja?

09:58.848 --> 10:00.600
The way they carry themselves,

10:01.809 --> 10:03.728
I think they know what they're doing.

10:06.522 --> 10:07.898
[inhales deeply]

10:09.066 --> 10:10.192
[sighs]

10:13.321 --> 10:14.780
[suspenseful music playing]

10:44.518 --> 10:47.772
- [man 1] Who's taking the next shift?
- [man 2] I think it's Kinoshita, sir.

10:47.855 --> 10:51.651
- [man 1] Oh, he's the new kid, right?
- [man 2] Yes, he is, but he's no good.

11:18.969 --> 11:20.471
[suspenseful music continues]

11:43.452 --> 11:44.870
[dramatic music sting]

12:07.393 --> 12:08.728
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir!

12:12.940 --> 12:14.358
[dramatic music playing]

13:00.404 --> 13:01.697
[music fades]

13:16.629 --> 13:19.840
[Mr. Gu] How is it
that we can't find a single lead?

13:19.924 --> 13:21.759
I combed through
Myeong-ja's favorite tea shops,

13:21.842 --> 13:24.804
restaurants, boutiques, shoe stores,
and any bar she would frequent,

13:24.887 --> 13:26.388
and no one has any idea where she is.

13:26.472 --> 13:28.307
No one has seen her at all, huh?

13:28.390 --> 13:31.769
Out of desperation I even went
to the rickshaw offices over there.

13:31.852 --> 13:33.354
They knew nothing at all.

13:33.437 --> 13:35.856
They said no one has seen Myeong-ja
or given her a ride.

13:35.940 --> 13:37.942
Ah, jeez. What do we do now, huh?

13:38.025 --> 13:40.110
She is nowhere to be found, yeah.

13:40.194 --> 13:43.405
It's like she evaporated into thin air.
Disappeared, up and gone.

13:44.448 --> 13:45.574
Everybody leaves a trace.

13:45.658 --> 13:48.035
Doesn't matter where they run off,
there's always a clue.

13:48.118 --> 13:50.162
We just have to find what that clue is.

13:50.871 --> 13:52.414
[whimsical music playing]

13:52.915 --> 13:57.044
By the way, is that really
how Ishikawa told them to tail us? Huh?

13:57.127 --> 13:58.796
They must think we're fools!

13:58.879 --> 14:02.341
That's probably the most obvious tail
I've ever witnessed in my life.

14:02.842 --> 14:06.470
It's so obvious that it's difficult
for me to pretend that I'm oblivious.

14:06.554 --> 14:08.889
- [man 1] What's going on?
- [man 2] Why are they fighting?

14:08.973 --> 14:11.392
- Anyone see what happened?
- Has he lost his mind?

14:12.309 --> 14:14.311
- [blow landing]
- [groans]

14:15.229 --> 14:16.522
Answer me now, kid!

14:16.605 --> 14:18.816
What color is
the pot I'm holding right here?

14:19.441 --> 14:20.317
It's, um,

14:21.193 --> 14:22.278
the color white.

14:22.361 --> 14:25.990
And what do you call
white porcelain in Joseon, huh?

14:26.574 --> 14:27.992
Baekja, sir.

14:29.493 --> 14:30.619
All right. So, then…

14:32.663 --> 14:33.581
what is this?

14:35.124 --> 14:38.252
It's baekja! So,
are you going to let me sell this, huh?

14:41.088 --> 14:42.172
[Tae-sang] Let's see.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.550
How should I put this?

14:45.050 --> 14:47.720
This looks a little too shoddy
to be called fine porcelain.

14:47.803 --> 14:50.931
Seems to be just some regular, old,
ordinary pottery to me, not baekja.

14:51.015 --> 14:53.893
How come I paid
over a hundred won for that thing, then?

14:54.727 --> 14:55.561
No idea.

14:56.186 --> 14:58.188
Then how much will your little pawn shop

14:58.939 --> 15:00.024
let me sell it for?

15:00.107 --> 15:04.361
Can you prove its authenticity?
A receipt or certificate would work.

15:04.445 --> 15:05.446
[man gasps]

15:07.865 --> 15:08.908
I don't have either.

15:13.245 --> 15:17.291
So you just paid 100 won for a pot
that hardly holds people's urine,

15:17.374 --> 15:19.084
but you did not get a certificate?

15:19.793 --> 15:23.464
Well, then, I guess it's clear
that you have been properly scammed.

15:23.547 --> 15:28.052
This is a matter for the police bureau,
not a pawnshop. Sorry I can't help you.

15:31.805 --> 15:33.057
Listen, Master Jang.

15:33.891 --> 15:36.518
How about you just do me a favor
and take this thing?

15:36.602 --> 15:40.773
We all know that Commissioner Ishikawa
is planning to confiscate everything.

15:40.856 --> 15:41.774
We'll see about that.

15:41.857 --> 15:44.985
All the rumors suggest otherwise,
so you better reconsider.

15:45.069 --> 15:48.405
We all suspect your golden pawnshop
will be getting a new owner.

15:48.489 --> 15:50.074
If you're losing everything anyway,

15:50.157 --> 15:53.202
why do you care
if there's an extra piss pot in here, huh?

15:54.745 --> 15:56.038
[chuckles]

15:57.039 --> 15:59.166
Listen, you little shit,
what's your problem?

15:59.667 --> 16:03.837
- Who are you to talk to me like this, huh?
- What? Who you calling "little shit"?

16:03.921 --> 16:06.423
How about you stop disrupting my business
and leave now?

16:06.507 --> 16:08.634
You're gonna get hurt if you keep this up.

16:08.717 --> 16:11.595
Oh, and your stupid little
tough guy way of speaking?

16:11.679 --> 16:14.431
I'm embarrassed for you.
Worst I've ever heard.

16:14.515 --> 16:16.558
Ah, you jackass! [grunts]

16:17.101 --> 16:18.018
You're dead!

16:20.270 --> 16:21.480
Hey!

16:21.563 --> 16:22.731
[tense music playing]

16:25.526 --> 16:26.360
[sighs]

16:26.443 --> 16:27.861
[panting]

16:32.032 --> 16:33.242
[music fades]

16:35.911 --> 16:39.248
I am the owner
of the House of Golden Treasure.

16:39.748 --> 16:42.418
That will always be the case.
You got that?

16:42.501 --> 16:45.004
So if you're gonna come in here
and cause a disturbance,

16:45.087 --> 16:47.423
or if you're even gonna
think of robbing me,

16:47.506 --> 16:49.800
get ready for one
of the following two things.

16:49.883 --> 16:52.344
You're gonna die
or get very close to dying.

16:52.428 --> 16:53.762
Ah…

16:55.097 --> 16:57.725
What's it gonna… be, samurai?

16:57.808 --> 17:00.269
Huh? I don't have all day.
My arms are shaking.

17:00.352 --> 17:04.023
My arms are feeling a bit heavy, see? See?
Look, look, look. Look.

17:04.815 --> 17:05.858
Hey.

17:07.192 --> 17:08.360
You might wanna leave now.

17:10.320 --> 17:11.405
[groans]

17:14.324 --> 17:15.701
[footsteps receding]

17:16.577 --> 17:18.120
- Move!
- Outta the way!

17:18.203 --> 17:19.455
- Move out of the way!
- Move!

17:19.538 --> 17:20.831
[crowd gasping]

17:21.707 --> 17:22.583
[sighs]

17:25.210 --> 17:26.462
Let's go.

17:28.839 --> 17:30.966
[woman] Out of the way. Get out of here!

17:34.720 --> 17:37.056
From now on,
we must all stay vigilant, okay?

17:37.681 --> 17:38.557
What?

17:39.975 --> 17:41.393
What do you mean by that?

17:41.477 --> 17:43.437
He means if we don't find Myeong-ja,

17:43.520 --> 17:45.898
thugs like that samurai bunch
are gonna keep coming around

17:45.981 --> 17:47.691
and causing trouble for us.

17:49.026 --> 17:50.569
[Mrs. Nawol] Which reminds me.

17:54.406 --> 17:57.284
They found the place
Myeong-ja is thought to have last visited.

17:57.785 --> 17:58.619
What?

17:59.119 --> 18:00.579
[mysterious music playing]

18:07.669 --> 18:11.715
So we found the rickshaw puller
who gave Myeong-ja a ride last week.

18:13.050 --> 18:15.469
What?! No way. That can't be.
That's not possible, huh?

18:15.552 --> 18:16.470
I… I already told you,

18:16.553 --> 18:19.264
I went to the Spring Moon Hall offices
and spoke to every guy!

18:19.348 --> 18:20.974
None of the rickshaw pullers
saw Myeong-Ja.

18:21.058 --> 18:22.893
I double-checked with all our sources!

18:22.976 --> 18:25.479
Well, he doesn't work
for Spring Moon Hall, Mr. Gu.

18:27.523 --> 18:28.398
What did you find out?

18:28.482 --> 18:30.901
You said that there's a chance
she could be dead.

18:31.944 --> 18:34.363
So we looked around
to see who the killer might be.

18:34.863 --> 18:36.365
There was one person we thought of.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.741
[ominous music sting]

18:37.825 --> 18:39.827
[suspenseful music playing]

18:55.008 --> 18:56.552
[woman] Where's Dr. Takahashi?

18:56.635 --> 18:59.680
He's ill and says he needs
three to four days to rest, ma'am.

19:02.766 --> 19:04.226
[Tae-sang] Lady Yukiko Maeda.

19:07.271 --> 19:09.857
You're saying she was
the last person to see Myeon-ja?

19:09.940 --> 19:12.776
Yes, Myeong-ja was called over
to Ishikawa's house.

19:12.860 --> 19:15.362
She stayed half an hour,
then she was sent somewhere else.

19:16.321 --> 19:17.364
Where'd she go?

19:17.948 --> 19:19.116
Ongseong Hospital.

19:19.950 --> 19:22.035
Ongseong… Ongseong Hospital?

19:22.619 --> 19:23.954
And you're sure of that?

19:24.037 --> 19:25.664
[engine starts]

19:25.747 --> 19:27.124
[man squealing]

19:29.543 --> 19:32.171
- [tires screech]
- [man yelling fearfully]

19:32.838 --> 19:35.382
Please stop! Let me down! [panting]

19:35.465 --> 19:38.177
You are certain
she was sent to Ongseong Hospital, then?

19:38.260 --> 19:39.845
Yes! That's where she is!

19:39.928 --> 19:41.889
It was Ongseong Hospital, I'm positive!

19:41.972 --> 19:43.473
I swear on my father

19:43.557 --> 19:44.975
and on my mother!

19:45.475 --> 19:48.437
The woman you're looking for
is there, I swear to you, okay?

19:48.520 --> 19:51.273
I swear that's where she is.
That's where I took her!

19:53.275 --> 19:54.568
Since Myeong-ja disappeared

19:54.651 --> 19:57.779
after the rickshaw puller dropped her off
at Ongseong Hospital,

19:57.863 --> 20:01.450
it's possible that she might be
held captive somewhere inside of there.

20:01.533 --> 20:04.119
Seriously, that is ridiculous, okay?
That makes no sense.

20:04.203 --> 20:05.746
What about it doesn't make sense?

20:05.829 --> 20:09.958
You must not know it's almost impossible
to get admitted. Japanese only.

20:10.042 --> 20:12.753
If you aren't part
of the Japanese military, the police,

20:12.836 --> 20:15.422
or the government-general's office,
you're not getting in.

20:15.505 --> 20:17.925
And you think
a Joseon courtesan was let inside?

20:18.008 --> 20:22.054
She would've needed a powerful connection
to even get past the front gate, okay?

20:23.263 --> 20:27.100
What if Lady Maeda arranged it?
What if she has something to do with this?

20:27.184 --> 20:29.144
And why would she do that, huh?

20:29.228 --> 20:31.772
You really believe Lady Maeda
would help out a girl like Myeong-Ja?

20:31.855 --> 20:33.273
Why would she? For what reason?

20:33.357 --> 20:35.734
We'll figure it out
once we're in the hospital.

20:35.817 --> 20:38.153
[Mr. Gu] What's the matter with you?
Did you not hear me?

20:38.237 --> 20:41.323
I just told you all
that we can't get in without a connection.

20:41.406 --> 20:43.659
Well, I heard that Master Jang
has quite a few connections.

20:46.078 --> 20:47.829
Would a hospital visit be
too hard for you?

20:47.913 --> 20:49.665
[chuckles]

20:52.459 --> 20:54.962
Well, I am in contact
with a few Joseon folks

20:55.045 --> 20:56.463
who can pass through no problem.

20:56.546 --> 20:58.548
Can you get us in or not?

20:58.632 --> 21:00.300
You'll just have to wait and see.

21:00.384 --> 21:01.343
I've had enough.

21:01.426 --> 21:03.804
If you can't figure it out,
we'll find a way to get in.

21:03.887 --> 21:07.224
Oh, you're impatient, aren't you?
Who said I couldn't figure it out?

21:07.307 --> 21:08.684
That's not what I was saying.

21:08.767 --> 21:11.603
I'm saying we just…
we plan it all out, that's all.

21:11.687 --> 21:14.898
You gotta plan things, not just improvise.
Always plan things out.

21:16.441 --> 21:18.318
[whimsical music playing]

21:24.324 --> 21:25.909
Do I got something on my face?

21:27.869 --> 21:29.913
[whimsical music continues]

21:30.914 --> 21:31.915
Huh? Oh.

21:38.005 --> 21:39.548
[Mrs. Nawol] Now what are you doing?

21:39.631 --> 21:41.758
Ah. Give these clothes
for them to change into.

21:41.842 --> 21:43.218
Why? What are you planning?

21:43.302 --> 21:45.262
How dare those sleuths doubt me.

21:45.345 --> 21:47.389
I'll show them
how shrewd and meticulous I am.

21:47.472 --> 21:49.349
I'm gonna show 'em, just watch.

21:49.433 --> 21:51.601
What is the money for?
What are you up to now?

21:52.269 --> 21:53.353
What do you think?

21:53.979 --> 21:56.857
There's nothing that money can't do, hmm?

22:04.990 --> 22:06.408
- What's this?
- Money.

22:07.784 --> 22:08.618
That's what it is.

22:09.494 --> 22:12.289
I don't care if you use it
for the independence movement or whatever.

22:12.372 --> 22:15.751
Spend it how you wish.
Do what you want with it. It's your money.

22:17.669 --> 22:19.671
You better tell me what you're up to.

22:24.051 --> 22:26.470
- Can I be you for a minute?
- What do you mean?

22:26.553 --> 22:30.223
I'm going to Ongseong Hospital.
I need to borrow your ID so I can get in.

22:30.724 --> 22:34.102
I know your family's
some of the only Joseons allowed to go in.

22:34.186 --> 22:35.103
Why?

22:35.771 --> 22:36.730
You feeling sick?

22:37.439 --> 22:38.482
No, I feel good, thank you.

22:38.565 --> 22:39.441
Oh.

22:40.317 --> 22:43.737
If this is concerning Ishikawa, I'm out.
No, thank you.

22:44.404 --> 22:45.447
[sighs]

22:47.324 --> 22:50.827
Just do me this favor as… a close friend.

22:50.911 --> 22:53.580
That is, if you still think of me
as your friend.

22:53.663 --> 22:56.083
I wanna know
who you're helping out, Tae-sang.

22:56.583 --> 22:59.044
If I'm lending you an ID,
I need to know what's going on.

22:59.127 --> 23:01.922
I'd worry about what could happen
if you become involved.

23:02.005 --> 23:05.801
You come here wanting to use my ID,
yet you're the one worried about me?

23:06.802 --> 23:07.886
Can I borrow your ID?

23:09.471 --> 23:13.809
[sighs] I wish you could use at least
some of that passion to help our cause.

23:13.892 --> 23:14.893
[Tae-sang chuckles]

23:16.103 --> 23:18.355
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply] I'm sorry,

23:18.438 --> 23:21.316
but I don't hope or daydream
about independence

23:21.400 --> 23:23.193
when this is all we've ever known.

23:24.194 --> 23:26.196
The king couldn't stop Japan
from taking over.

23:26.279 --> 23:27.948
What makes you any different?

23:28.448 --> 23:30.617
There's only one thing
I'm concerned about.

23:31.243 --> 23:33.203
I only wanna survive all this.

23:33.870 --> 23:36.706
Making it as long as I can,
preferably in one piece.

23:37.666 --> 23:38.625
So, uh…

23:40.669 --> 23:41.795
help me do this, okay?

23:41.878 --> 23:43.004
[chuckles softly]

23:43.088 --> 23:44.381
[whimsical music playing]

23:45.257 --> 23:46.216
[sighs]

23:48.510 --> 23:50.303
Return it as soon as you're done.

23:50.387 --> 23:52.013
[melodic instrumental music playing]

23:52.097 --> 23:52.931
[chuckles]

23:53.014 --> 23:54.057
I will indeed.

23:54.850 --> 23:56.059
[music fades]

24:08.071 --> 24:09.322
[Mr. Gu] So how'd it go?

24:10.866 --> 24:13.201
The sleuths, where are they?
Are they coming yet?

24:14.119 --> 24:15.287
[Mr. Gu] Ah…

24:15.370 --> 24:18.748
- Oh, they're over there.
- [woman] That one's pretty too! Right?

24:20.459 --> 24:22.085
Thank you. They're so colorful!

24:22.169 --> 24:23.503
[romantic music playing]

24:53.992 --> 24:55.118
[Mr. Gu clears throat]

24:56.953 --> 24:59.623
- Shall we go now?
- What? Oh!

24:59.706 --> 25:02.751
- [father] We don't have all day.
- [Tae-sang] Yes. Right.

25:02.834 --> 25:04.377
Let's go. Please get in.

25:13.094 --> 25:16.598
Ah, so helping a lady into the car
is just good manners here.

25:18.016 --> 25:19.351
Well, I don't need it.

25:26.358 --> 25:27.275
[Tae-sang sighs]

25:29.861 --> 25:31.071
[engine starts]

25:31.154 --> 25:32.364
All right, everyone, let's go.

25:32.447 --> 25:34.115
[adventurous music playing]

25:48.880 --> 25:50.966
[reverential music playing]

25:57.097 --> 25:57.931
ID, please.

26:01.059 --> 26:02.310
[Mr. Gu] This is my master.

26:02.811 --> 26:05.272
Sir, do you know the, uh,
the Bugang Company?

26:05.355 --> 26:07.065
Sure you do. His father owns it.

26:11.945 --> 26:13.446
[guard] Are they all with you?

26:14.406 --> 26:15.490
Uh…

26:15.574 --> 26:17.659
The other two in the back?
Both are family.

26:17.742 --> 26:19.995
They are my master's fiancée
and her father.

26:25.917 --> 26:28.670
Oh, it's almost time
for our appointment. Oh my!

26:30.422 --> 26:32.007
Can we go ahead, please, sir?

26:32.090 --> 26:34.801
Dr. Takahashi absolutely hates it
when we're not on time,

26:34.884 --> 26:37.512
so just let us through
or we'll be late, huh? [chuckles]

26:37.596 --> 26:39.598
That's not my concern, dirty Josenjing.

26:40.181 --> 26:41.516
Okay, let them through.

26:41.600 --> 26:42.892
Thank you, good sir.

26:48.481 --> 26:50.609
- [guard] Wait! Hold on!
- [tires screech]

26:59.409 --> 27:00.327
[guard sighs]

27:06.875 --> 27:09.753
- Here you go. You forgot this.
- Ah, the ID! I almost forgot!

27:09.836 --> 27:11.546
I'm really thankful for you, sir.

27:15.592 --> 27:17.177
[engine starts]

27:17.844 --> 27:20.388
[rickshaw puller] Almost there.
Any minute now.

27:23.224 --> 27:24.851
[foreboding music playing]

27:41.868 --> 27:42.911
[music fades]

27:44.871 --> 27:45.789
Ongseong Hospital?

27:45.872 --> 27:49.876
Yes, sir. He's been seen entering
the facility with a few other Josenjings.

27:50.460 --> 27:53.713
Tell me, sir.
Should we follow them around?

27:56.091 --> 27:57.217
[sighs]

28:08.895 --> 28:10.480
[intriguing music playing]

28:13.525 --> 28:14.526
[door opens]

28:18.405 --> 28:20.573
RECORDS ROOM

28:20.657 --> 28:22.575
[indistinct chattering in distance]

28:41.177 --> 28:43.179
I'd like to see Dr. Takahashi, please.
Thank you.

28:44.180 --> 28:45.515
Did you say Dr. Takahashi?

28:46.808 --> 28:49.018
[Jun-taek] Our family physician
is Dr. Takahashi.

28:49.102 --> 28:51.062
I don't think he'll be there today.

28:51.146 --> 28:53.940
He has tennis lessons
every Thursday afternoon.

28:55.442 --> 28:56.443
It'll work out, then.

28:56.526 --> 28:59.279
Sorry, sir.
I don't think that he's in today.

28:59.362 --> 29:02.657
Oh, are you certain that's true?
He told me I could see him today.

29:03.324 --> 29:05.285
Would you mind checking again for me?

29:06.411 --> 29:08.371
- Yes, sir. I'll check for you.
- Thanks.

29:17.213 --> 29:18.798
[suspenseful music playing]

29:23.261 --> 29:25.722
[pained yelling] Oh, my stomach!

29:25.805 --> 29:26.848
Oh!

29:26.931 --> 29:28.600
- [pained yelling]
- [man gasps]

29:28.683 --> 29:31.060
- Sir, are you all right?
- [pained yelping]

29:31.144 --> 29:33.229
[nurse] Sir? Are you all right?

29:33.313 --> 29:34.606
What happened, sir?

29:34.689 --> 29:36.107
- Tell us what happened!
- My stomach!

29:36.191 --> 29:37.734
- What happened?
- [nurse] What did you do?

29:37.817 --> 29:39.277
- [screaming]
- Get him on the ground.

29:39.360 --> 29:41.488
- Where does it hurt?
- Just hang on!

29:41.571 --> 29:43.072
[Mr. Gu] It's coming out!

29:43.156 --> 29:45.074
[Tae-sang] What's coming out
of your bottom?

29:45.158 --> 29:48.077
- [Mr. Gu] Oh, it hurts! It hurts so much!
- [Tae-sang] What's coming out?

29:48.161 --> 29:49.662
- [Mr. Gu] It's coming out!
- What is?

29:55.835 --> 29:57.587
- Help me!
- [nurse] Sir, just relax!

29:57.670 --> 30:01.007
Is there anyone that can help us?
Help us! Doctor!

30:01.090 --> 30:03.635
[Mr. Gu yelling in agony]

30:05.845 --> 30:06.763
They're getting help!

30:06.846 --> 30:08.515
[mysterious music playing]

30:11.976 --> 30:13.520
Akiko…

30:14.687 --> 30:15.688
where are you?

30:21.194 --> 30:22.403
Akiko…

30:32.247 --> 30:33.331
[man] Who are you?

30:40.463 --> 30:41.798
What are you doing in here?

30:44.008 --> 30:45.009
Sorry, sir.

30:46.761 --> 30:48.221
I must've taken a wrong turn.

30:48.304 --> 30:50.265
You must have taken a wrong turn,

30:50.348 --> 30:52.976
so you started flipping
through the records?

30:53.059 --> 30:55.770
Actually, I'm looking for
a friend hospitalized here.

30:56.604 --> 30:58.189
But I don't know where she is.

31:03.319 --> 31:04.487
[ominous music playing]

31:04.571 --> 31:06.072
I know you're from Joseon. I can tell.

31:07.031 --> 31:08.366
Let's not make a scene.

31:08.950 --> 31:10.368
So I'll just leave quietly, okay?

31:13.580 --> 31:14.414
Is that all right?

31:14.998 --> 31:18.293
Reveal who you are first.
Tell me who you are, and I'll let you go.

31:22.171 --> 31:23.298
[door opens]

31:24.799 --> 31:25.675
[gasps]

31:25.758 --> 31:27.927
Listen, it's better to be alive than dead.

31:28.011 --> 31:29.804
[ominous music playing]

31:33.600 --> 31:36.519
By chance, are you two from Manchuria?

31:38.146 --> 31:39.480
Got a name, sir?

31:39.564 --> 31:40.773
[inhales shakily]

31:41.649 --> 31:42.567
[sighs]

31:46.529 --> 31:49.490
The doctor will be here soon.
It's gonna be all right

31:49.574 --> 31:52.076
I think the doctor's here.
The doctor's here now.

31:52.160 --> 31:53.828
[pained yelling]

31:53.912 --> 31:55.121
[Tae-sang] Uh…

31:55.204 --> 31:56.247
[fearful yelping]

31:56.331 --> 31:58.917
This will help alleviate
some of the pain for now.

31:59.918 --> 32:01.002
[whimpering]

32:01.085 --> 32:02.962
- Take off his jacket.
- Yes, Doctor.

32:03.046 --> 32:05.673
- I can't! I can't! No! No! Let me go!
- [Tae-sang] No.

32:05.757 --> 32:07.216
[Mr. Gu] No, stop! Stop! No!

32:07.300 --> 32:09.010
No, stop! [yelping]

32:09.093 --> 32:11.346
Please, don't let him do this!
[whimpering]

32:11.429 --> 32:12.388
No! No!

32:12.472 --> 32:14.682
[terrified yelping]

32:14.766 --> 32:16.351
Please, Master!

32:16.434 --> 32:18.186
- [doctor] Come on! Quickly!
- Yes, Doctor.

32:18.269 --> 32:19.771
It'll make you feel better.

32:19.854 --> 32:21.147
I can't! No! No!

32:21.230 --> 32:22.482
- Mr. Gu!
- [Mr. Gu] Stop! Stop it!

32:22.565 --> 32:24.150
Come here, you bastard!

32:25.068 --> 32:27.654
Don't let him do this! [whimpering]

32:29.030 --> 32:30.531
- Why, huh?
- [Tae-sang] Huh?

32:30.615 --> 32:31.950
[Mr. Gu whimpering]

32:32.033 --> 32:34.285
Oh! Oh, hold on. It's okay.
Just hold on a second.

32:34.369 --> 32:36.245
Hold on! Just hold on, huh?

32:37.747 --> 32:38.623
Oh…

32:40.541 --> 32:42.335
- Huh?
- What?

32:42.418 --> 32:43.753
The pain suddenly disappeared!

32:43.836 --> 32:45.546
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

32:46.255 --> 32:47.423
How is this possible?

32:47.507 --> 32:50.051
- It doesn't hurt at all anymore!
- Well, are you sure?

32:50.134 --> 32:52.387
I'm suddenly healed
because of what the doctor did!

32:52.470 --> 32:53.888
That's amazing!

32:53.972 --> 32:55.139
[crowd gasping]

32:55.765 --> 32:58.726
How can we ever thank you?
You're an amazing doctor.

32:58.810 --> 33:00.144
[crowd murmuring]

33:00.228 --> 33:01.646
[whimsical music playing]

33:08.861 --> 33:09.779
Great visit.

33:10.780 --> 33:12.281
[shocked muttering]

33:13.616 --> 33:15.743
Were you gonna let him
actually give me the shot?

33:16.244 --> 33:17.870
What matters is he didn't do it.

33:20.123 --> 33:21.624
[distant gunshot echoing]

33:21.708 --> 33:22.834
[man 1] What was that?

33:23.584 --> 33:26.838
- What's going on? Where did it come from?
- [woman 1] Please don't be alarmed.

33:26.921 --> 33:30.341
The military base nearby
must be holding a target practice.

33:30.425 --> 33:32.885
- [woman 2] Whoa, that was scary.
- [Mr. Gu] That's strange.

33:32.969 --> 33:35.263
It came from under the building.
I wonder what's down there.

33:35.847 --> 33:38.266
Let's just keep moving. This way.

33:38.349 --> 33:40.351
[unsettling music playing]

33:46.607 --> 33:49.318
- Why did you open fire?
- [soldier 1] We couldn't capture it.

33:49.402 --> 33:51.946
Two of our soldiers were attacked
before we even got to the door.

33:52.030 --> 33:55.199
One corporal is still alive
on the floor. What should we do?

33:55.283 --> 33:56.409
Please help me!

33:57.160 --> 33:58.911
- Please help…
- [snarling]

33:58.995 --> 34:00.079
[guns cocking]

34:01.539 --> 34:03.249
[snarling]

34:03.916 --> 34:04.751
Should we open fire?

34:06.627 --> 34:08.755
[pained yelling]

34:09.464 --> 34:10.757
[screaming]

34:11.424 --> 34:12.300
[wailing]

34:12.383 --> 34:14.510
Sir, should I go
rescue the corporal or not?

34:14.594 --> 34:16.804
Remain still. Remain where you are.

34:16.888 --> 34:18.639
If I don't get him, he could die!

34:18.723 --> 34:20.808
Shh! Do not shoot the creature.

34:20.892 --> 34:22.727
I need that creature alive.
Do you understand?

34:23.686 --> 34:26.939
This experiment is important to us.
This creature is vital for us.

34:27.023 --> 34:27.857
You got that?

34:29.567 --> 34:32.070
Lt. Kato, what is that?

34:32.153 --> 34:33.529
[slithering]

34:33.613 --> 34:35.990
[soldier 1] What is that thing?
What do we do?!

34:36.074 --> 34:37.492
[soldier 2] Please save me.

34:38.034 --> 34:39.994
[creature snarling, growling]

34:40.078 --> 34:41.996
[soldier 2 gasping fearfully]

34:42.080 --> 34:43.039
Please save me!

34:44.499 --> 34:45.666
Please help!

34:45.750 --> 34:47.210
Please help me.

34:47.293 --> 34:48.336
Please save me…

34:48.419 --> 34:50.171
[creature snarling]

34:50.254 --> 34:51.506
[low growling]

34:52.590 --> 34:55.051
[soldier 2] Please,
I'm begging you! Please!

34:55.134 --> 34:56.803
Please help me! [groans]

34:57.345 --> 34:58.221
[scales creaking]

34:59.847 --> 35:01.474
[soldier 2 whimpering]

35:02.141 --> 35:03.434
[grunts, gasps]

35:04.227 --> 35:05.269
[gasping]

35:12.068 --> 35:14.320
- Let him go!
- Stop, soldier. Hold your fire!

35:14.403 --> 35:15.696
[soldier yells]

35:17.615 --> 35:18.825
[choked gasping]

35:23.287 --> 35:24.956
[choked breathing]

35:26.833 --> 35:28.126
[whimpers, yelps]

35:28.209 --> 35:30.670
[panicked gasping]

35:31.212 --> 35:32.171
[bones crunching]

35:32.255 --> 35:33.256
[flesh squelching]

35:33.339 --> 35:34.924
[reverential music playing]

35:38.010 --> 35:39.178
Magnificent.

35:41.514 --> 35:43.224
[snarling]

35:46.102 --> 35:48.187
What a magnificent goddess you are!

35:48.271 --> 35:50.022
[dramatic music playing]

35:55.236 --> 35:57.780
[creature roaring]

36:01.242 --> 36:02.827
[dramatic music continues]

36:05.997 --> 36:07.290
[music fades]

36:22.722 --> 36:23.723
[Tae-sang sighs]

36:24.724 --> 36:28.394
What's this? What are you doing right now?
Why do you have extra clothes?

36:28.477 --> 36:30.980
My father and I are spending the night
at the hospital.

36:31.063 --> 36:32.273
What?

36:32.356 --> 36:34.400
Uh, wait. Are we staying with you too?

36:34.483 --> 36:37.737
You two will just be in our way,
so you should leave now while you can.

36:38.696 --> 36:41.032
I'm not leaving until you tell me
what you're planning to do.

36:44.410 --> 36:46.662
Behind the hospital is a military ward.

36:47.330 --> 36:49.582
I also heard
the basement is more of a prison.

36:50.082 --> 36:51.000
I've also been told

36:51.083 --> 36:54.295
that they transfer Joseon people
from Seodaemun Prison to here.

36:54.378 --> 36:56.088
But those who are sent to the basement…

36:57.340 --> 37:00.092
- Well, I heard they never come back.
- [Mr. Gu gasps]

37:01.385 --> 37:02.762
Wait, is Myeong-ja down there?

37:03.387 --> 37:05.139
Well, that's what
we're planning to find out.

37:05.223 --> 37:06.349
Excuse me?

37:07.642 --> 37:09.977
When, might I ask,
did you happen to learn all of this?

37:10.061 --> 37:10.978
[door opens]

37:13.314 --> 37:15.441
[janitor breathing heavily]

37:15.524 --> 37:18.027
There's some unusual movement
in the military ward right now.

37:18.110 --> 37:19.862
You should come back
and try this another day.

37:20.738 --> 37:22.406
We don't have time to come back.

37:22.490 --> 37:25.076
So you just show us the way,
and we'll do the rest.

37:29.038 --> 37:30.414
[Mr. Gu exhales sharply]

37:33.709 --> 37:34.752
[Tae-sang] Wait, I--

37:39.006 --> 37:40.049
Just… [sighs]

37:40.132 --> 37:44.011
Just what is going on right now?
The plan was to go in and get out.

37:44.095 --> 37:46.097
What did this janitor say
to make you change your--

37:46.180 --> 37:47.640
They took my brother a year ago.

37:47.723 --> 37:50.601
He was at Seodaemun Prison
when they transferred him to Ongseong.

37:51.644 --> 37:53.896
I was told
he was brought here for a fever.

37:53.980 --> 37:55.731
That's when I lost all contact.

37:55.815 --> 37:58.734
I looked everywhere for him,
but there's no record of him anywhere.

37:58.818 --> 38:02.405
My goodness. So you got a job here
to look for your missing brother?

38:02.488 --> 38:05.950
Why should I believe you?
You're a complete stranger to me.

38:06.033 --> 38:07.410
[janitor inhales deeply]

38:09.912 --> 38:10.746
[Mr. Gu gasps]

38:15.960 --> 38:16.794
What does that mean?

38:16.877 --> 38:19.088
It's the symbol for the Patriotic Society.

38:20.298 --> 38:22.425
It's a resistance group.
Did you really not know that?

38:25.177 --> 38:28.222
You should head out while you can.
We'll send a message

38:28.306 --> 38:31.142
on whether or not Myeong-ja is being
held captive in the basement.

38:32.852 --> 38:34.895
- But I thought--
- [Chae-ok] Okay, I'm ready.

38:35.479 --> 38:36.731
[janitor] Then follow me.

38:38.065 --> 38:39.066
Hey, wait a minute.

38:39.150 --> 38:41.819
Oh, um, thank you for the clothes.

38:41.902 --> 38:43.988
That's not what I meant
when I asked you to wait.

38:47.992 --> 38:50.244
Well, did… did you have
something else to say?

38:52.788 --> 38:53.831
What is it?

38:54.999 --> 38:55.833
Just say it.

39:01.130 --> 39:01.964
[Tae-sang] Well…

39:03.382 --> 39:04.842
I, uh, I just, um…

39:07.595 --> 39:11.057
This plan of yours is completely reckless.
In fact, it's a bad idea.

39:12.350 --> 39:15.186
Let's be a little more reasonable.
You should really think this through.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.063
You gave us the time frame.

39:18.606 --> 39:22.109
We have till the cherry blossoms lose
their flowers. That's what you told us.

39:22.610 --> 39:26.155
With cherry blossoms, they bloom quickly,
but just as fast, they're gone.

39:26.238 --> 39:28.783
So we have to act now.
That's my plan here.

39:28.866 --> 39:31.952
I'm not okay with this. There's no reason
to deviate from the original plan.

39:32.036 --> 39:34.205
You change your principles
on the situation.

39:35.164 --> 39:37.583
A change in plans
shouldn't be too hard for you.

39:38.376 --> 39:41.003
It's like… what did you call it again?
Having flexibility?

39:44.548 --> 39:47.718
We'll execute on our end…
and you do the same.

39:47.802 --> 39:49.095
Find Sachimoto for me.

39:49.887 --> 39:50.930
Will you do that?

39:52.807 --> 39:53.724
[father] Chae-ok.

39:54.433 --> 39:55.351
I'm coming.

39:59.647 --> 40:00.481
[door closes]

40:00.981 --> 40:04.235
Wow, they sure are quick
to take initiative, don't ya think?

40:04.318 --> 40:05.778
Huh? Don't you think so?

40:09.532 --> 40:11.158
[breathing heavily]

40:14.328 --> 40:15.579
[man] Hey, you!

40:16.455 --> 40:18.707
Visitors are not permitted
to be in this area.

40:19.208 --> 40:20.042
Who are you?

40:20.126 --> 40:22.670
Ah! I'm so sorry, sir.

40:22.753 --> 40:24.713
We were looking for the restroom
and got lost.

40:24.797 --> 40:26.715
- We should go now, Master.
- Yes.

40:27.591 --> 40:28.717
[man] Wait a second.

40:35.808 --> 40:37.643
Oh, there you are. I was looking for you.

40:41.480 --> 40:42.565
So I double-checked.

40:42.648 --> 40:45.651
Dr. Takahashi is unfortunately
out of the office today.

40:47.027 --> 40:48.737
Ah, he's not here, then?

40:48.821 --> 40:51.115
I guess I got the date confused for today.

40:51.949 --> 40:53.200
I'm so embarrassed.

40:53.284 --> 40:54.535
[man] Is he a patient?

40:55.744 --> 40:58.831
Yes, he is.
He's Dr. Takahashi's patient. I checked.

40:58.914 --> 41:00.708
[man clears throat]

41:01.333 --> 41:02.668
[Tae-sung chuckles softly]

41:03.294 --> 41:04.462
[siren blaring]

41:08.757 --> 41:10.092
You better leave now, sir.

41:12.261 --> 41:14.138
[man 2] This is an emergency.

41:14.221 --> 41:18.559
All visitors and outpatients
who have come in for appointments today

41:19.226 --> 41:20.686
must exit the premises.

41:21.187 --> 41:23.230
- [woman] What is going on?
- [man 2] I repeat.

41:24.773 --> 41:28.152
All visitors and outpatients
who have come in for appointments today

41:29.278 --> 41:30.613
must leave the building.

41:32.198 --> 41:34.033
Everyone, please leave the building.

41:38.496 --> 41:41.123
Lt. Kato, please give us an order.

41:41.207 --> 41:43.876
What do you want us to do?
The door will break any minute now!

41:46.420 --> 41:47.338
Lt. Kato!

41:48.422 --> 41:49.340
[soldier 1 gasps]

41:50.633 --> 41:52.259
We will proceed to Level 4.

41:53.511 --> 41:54.762
Retrieve the nitrogen.

41:54.845 --> 41:55.930
Yes, sir!

41:56.013 --> 41:57.890
The nitrogen, go grab it now!

41:57.973 --> 41:58.974
Yes, sir!

42:00.351 --> 42:02.561
[creature snarling ferociously]

42:02.645 --> 42:03.896
[dramatic music playing]

42:06.482 --> 42:08.400
I'll protect you. Don't you worry.

42:10.236 --> 42:13.113
We're gonna move you to a place
fit for the queen that you are.

42:13.197 --> 42:14.156
[creature snarls]

42:14.240 --> 42:15.699
[woman] What was that all about?

42:15.783 --> 42:16.951
[confused muttering]

42:17.701 --> 42:19.662
[Mr. Gu] I'm sure everything will be fine.

42:19.745 --> 42:21.747
They did say they were experts at this.

42:22.248 --> 42:24.291
Once they can confirm
Myeong-ja's in the hospital,

42:24.375 --> 42:25.251
they'll come back out.

42:26.669 --> 42:29.255
- Speaking of which…
- [Mr. Gu] Yes?

42:30.756 --> 42:33.384
It looks like
they are as devoted to their work as I am.

42:34.802 --> 42:36.971
[siren blaring in distance]

42:39.765 --> 42:42.476
- [siren continues]
- [suspenseful music playing]

42:58.158 --> 42:59.702
NO ENTRY

43:01.120 --> 43:02.538
NO ENTRY

43:03.956 --> 43:05.457
NO ENTRY

43:16.051 --> 43:17.553
[dramatic music continues]

43:36.363 --> 43:37.281
[Kato] Any movement?

43:38.115 --> 43:40.784
[solder 1] None, sir.
It seems to be fully asleep for now.

43:42.578 --> 43:43.912
[unsettling music playing]

44:02.097 --> 44:03.390
[gas hissing]

44:17.655 --> 44:19.114
[crate squeaking]

44:24.620 --> 44:26.955
[soldier 2] What is that?
What is all that?

44:27.039 --> 44:30.334
[soldier 3] Well, they look like
they're… spores of some kind.

44:31.085 --> 44:32.336
[Kato] It's anthrax.

44:32.836 --> 44:36.131
It's protecting itself,
even while it sleeps.

44:37.466 --> 44:40.552
- [solder 2] We've finished moving it, sir.
- [soldier 1] Close the door.

44:42.221 --> 44:43.347
[door slams closed]

44:52.940 --> 44:54.692
[Kato] We will proceed to Level 4.

44:54.775 --> 44:57.736
Don't forget to continuously
inject nitrogen during transportation.

44:57.820 --> 45:00.322
It's in a trance state
and can wake up in seconds.

45:00.406 --> 45:01.407
Let's all be careful.

45:01.490 --> 45:03.742
- [soldiers] Yes, sir!
- [soldier 1] Let's move!

45:04.785 --> 45:06.620
[tense music playing]

45:25.305 --> 45:26.473
[music intensifies]

45:49.288 --> 45:51.123
[creature breathing heavily]

45:53.584 --> 45:55.002
[creature growling softly]

45:57.171 --> 45:58.505
[music fades]

46:08.932 --> 46:10.517
[tense music playing]

46:19.610 --> 46:22.112
Hmm? It looks like a snowflake.

46:24.281 --> 46:25.574
It melts so quickly.

46:54.144 --> 46:55.103
[slow breathing]

46:55.187 --> 46:56.855
[suspenseful music playing]

46:58.357 --> 46:59.608
[breathing shakily]

47:07.241 --> 47:08.492
[girl whimpers]

47:08.575 --> 47:10.536
[pained gasping, yelping]

47:10.619 --> 47:11.912
[screaming]

47:13.580 --> 47:15.624
[pained screaming]

47:15.707 --> 47:17.376
[prisoners screaming in pain]

47:23.006 --> 47:24.424
[dramatic music playing]

47:24.508 --> 47:25.634
Is someone there?!

47:25.717 --> 47:28.178
- [fearful yelling]
- [prisoners screaming]

47:37.479 --> 47:38.730
[squealing]

47:42.651 --> 47:43.527
[panting]

47:43.610 --> 47:45.487
[prisoners screaming]

47:45.571 --> 47:46.989
[flesh sizzling]

47:50.367 --> 47:51.994
[pained screaming continues]

47:57.749 --> 47:59.751
[dramatic music intensifies]

48:00.544 --> 48:02.546
[prisoners screaming in pain]

48:07.426 --> 48:08.510
[Kato] Amazing.

48:09.511 --> 48:11.889
[prisoners screaming]

48:11.972 --> 48:13.348
[tense music playing]

48:17.227 --> 48:18.729
[all breathing heavily]

48:36.830 --> 48:39.833
Didn't you say the military ward
only held injured Japanese soldiers?

48:39.917 --> 48:42.169
Yes, they're kept
on the second and third floors, mainly.

48:42.252 --> 48:44.046
The first floor is usually
for administration,

48:44.129 --> 48:45.797
communications, and liaisons.

48:49.718 --> 48:51.845
It looks more like a military base
than a ward.

48:51.929 --> 48:55.515
[janitor] The security is so tight
that I'd never dare to go near that area.

48:56.016 --> 48:59.102
I'm only allowed into the ward
once every two days to clean.

48:59.686 --> 49:01.396
Why is that watchtower over there empty?

49:02.189 --> 49:05.692
A man fell to his death once
because the watchtower wasn't stable.

49:05.776 --> 49:08.570
They keep talking about renovating it,
but so far they haven't.

49:09.738 --> 49:11.239
Can you make it to that watchtower?

49:16.119 --> 49:19.206
Looks like it won't be easy…
but I can make it.

49:19.289 --> 49:20.916
- Be right back.
- [janitor] Hold on.

49:24.211 --> 49:25.295
Wait, don't--

49:25.379 --> 49:26.880
[suspenseful music playing]

50:07.504 --> 50:08.422
[door opening]

50:10.799 --> 50:11.675
[door closes]

50:15.345 --> 50:17.014
[suspenseful music intensifies]

50:41.079 --> 50:41.913
She disappeared.

50:49.463 --> 50:51.882
[breathing heavily]

51:12.652 --> 51:14.196
[ethereal music playing]

51:14.279 --> 51:16.156
[siren blaring]

51:25.248 --> 51:26.917
[military-style drumbeat]

51:28.710 --> 51:30.045
[footsteps approaching]

51:33.965 --> 51:36.176
- [soldier 1] Hurry, move! Quickly!
- [soldiers] Yes, sir!

51:36.259 --> 51:37.677
[dramatic music playing]

51:43.850 --> 51:46.728
- What should we do, sir?
- What are you doing? Get ready to move!

51:46.812 --> 51:48.021
- Move out!
- Sir!

51:48.105 --> 51:49.856
Move quickly! Hurry!

51:50.524 --> 51:52.109
Be quick about it. Go!

51:52.776 --> 51:54.861
- Load everything into truck four.
- Yes, sir.

51:55.487 --> 51:57.364
Move to the basement! Move!

51:58.740 --> 52:00.492
Move quickly! Let's go!

52:08.625 --> 52:10.127
[dramatic music playing]

52:26.268 --> 52:27.602
[music fades]

52:40.949 --> 52:42.450
[clock ticking]

52:45.036 --> 52:47.789
[inhales deeply, exhales slowly]

52:49.749 --> 52:51.585
[gentle instrumental music playing]

52:53.211 --> 52:54.462
[inhales nervously]

53:00.468 --> 53:02.179
You are still here, Master Jang?

53:06.725 --> 53:09.519
Goodness. Well, talk to me. What is it?

53:11.563 --> 53:13.148
I really don't understand it at all.

53:14.399 --> 53:15.483
What don't you understand?

53:16.735 --> 53:18.486
Why do I seem to be so worried?

53:19.279 --> 53:20.906
What are you worried about, huh?

53:27.871 --> 53:30.498
I mean, if we look
at the situation right now,

53:30.582 --> 53:34.127
Ishikawa basically has
my life in his hands.

53:34.211 --> 53:35.879
So if I cannot find Myeong-ja,

53:35.962 --> 53:38.798
then everything I own
will get completely confiscated.

53:38.882 --> 53:42.385
So it's very likely
that I could get dragged off into war.

53:42.469 --> 53:43.970
Oh, and not to mention

53:44.054 --> 53:46.848
the vultures and hyenas
circling the House of Golden Treasure,

53:46.932 --> 53:48.975
trying to pick off whatever they can.

53:51.061 --> 53:53.146
So why am I so…

53:55.148 --> 53:56.316
worried about her?

53:56.900 --> 53:58.443
Are you talking about the sleuth girl?

53:59.361 --> 54:00.195
Who?

54:00.278 --> 54:01.988
The woman you mentioned just now.

54:02.072 --> 54:03.073
Oh, her?

54:05.575 --> 54:06.743
Did I mention her just now?

54:06.826 --> 54:08.536
Oh, how unfortunate.

54:09.246 --> 54:10.956
This man is so hopelessly in love.

54:11.039 --> 54:13.792
Whoa, whoa, whoa! In love?
Those are some strong words.

54:13.875 --> 54:15.252
I am Jang Tae-sang.

54:15.335 --> 54:18.463
Here in Gyeongseong, all the women
throw themselves at me, huh?

54:18.546 --> 54:21.633
Right now I'm Bukchon's hot guy.
And I'm not phased one bit.

54:21.716 --> 54:22.884
You sure about that?

54:24.094 --> 54:27.430
Usually you act like you're above
the women in Gyeongseong, but now

54:28.265 --> 54:29.766
something's changed, hmm?

54:30.350 --> 54:32.686
The first woman to ignore you,
and now you're in love.

54:32.769 --> 54:34.604
Ah, no, no! It is not like that.

54:34.688 --> 54:36.147
Okay, then please explain.

54:36.231 --> 54:38.191
Um, you know…

54:39.567 --> 54:42.279
it's called… How do I put it? Humanism?

54:42.362 --> 54:43.780
Humanism? Really?

54:43.863 --> 54:46.116
Yes, that's right. It's humanism.

54:46.199 --> 54:47.951
Love for all, uh…

54:48.785 --> 54:50.328
all of humankind. That's it.

54:50.412 --> 54:54.457
I often ponder and worry for everyone.
I care a lot more than you think, hmm?

54:54.541 --> 54:56.626
- Now you know.
- Wow, how refreshing.

54:56.710 --> 54:59.504
Okay, I shouldn't have left
her and her father alone.

54:59.587 --> 55:02.757
I should've made her leave that hospital
with me. Now she's in danger.

55:02.841 --> 55:05.010
Then how about you go find this Sachimoto?

55:06.177 --> 55:09.347
Instead of complaining,
why don't you make use of this time?

55:09.431 --> 55:11.766
If you really want to help her,
do something about it!

55:11.850 --> 55:15.729
How about you be the man I know you are
and find a way to fix all this?

55:20.734 --> 55:21.651
Okay, then.

55:24.446 --> 55:25.280
I'll fix this.

55:27.198 --> 55:28.116
Where are you off to?

55:28.199 --> 55:30.702
[Tae-sang] To do what I have to do,
in my own way.

55:42.505 --> 55:43.923
[Tae-sang breathing heavily]

55:47.719 --> 55:49.262
[groans] Why does he do this?

55:50.930 --> 55:54.684
There's no way I'm driving you around,
you got that? So leave me alone.

55:54.768 --> 55:55.685
[Tae-sang scoffs]

55:56.686 --> 55:59.898
Whatever. In that case,
just write this down.

55:59.981 --> 56:02.817
Sachimoto. He's a Japanese man,
about 35 years old.

56:04.903 --> 56:06.905
- I told you to write it down.
- Oh.

56:08.114 --> 56:09.449
He's a painter, an artist.

56:09.532 --> 56:12.660
I need you to tell Commissioner Ishikawa
to tell his men to search for him.

56:12.744 --> 56:15.330
Search all over Gyeongseong
for this Sachimoto guy.

56:15.413 --> 56:17.248
Tell him this guy is crucial in helping us

56:17.332 --> 56:19.542
locate the whereabouts
of his dear Myeong-Ja.

56:19.626 --> 56:20.710
- Yes.
- Okay!

56:34.057 --> 56:35.058
[mutters angrily]

56:36.351 --> 56:37.435
[sighs]

56:38.144 --> 56:39.145
Here you are.

56:39.771 --> 56:40.605
[woman] Mm-hmm.

56:40.688 --> 56:42.482
[relaxing piano music playing]

56:50.949 --> 56:52.117
Who is that you're drawing?

56:55.495 --> 56:57.622
Oh, uh, I'm sorry, sir.

56:58.581 --> 57:01.626
I didn't mean to pry.
Just she looks like she's from Joseon.

57:04.170 --> 57:06.506
How could you tell… she was?

57:08.466 --> 57:10.385
[server] It's the parting of her hair.

57:10.468 --> 57:12.345
- [Sachimoto sighs]
- [server chuckles]

57:13.304 --> 57:14.180
I didn't know that.

57:16.349 --> 57:18.518
You know, you're quite talented at that.

57:19.894 --> 57:22.397
- Are you employed as a painter?
- [chuckles wryly]

57:32.740 --> 57:34.659
[vendor] Breaking news! Breaking news!

57:34.742 --> 57:36.619
Ongseong Hospital
will be closed indefinitely!

57:36.703 --> 57:39.789
Ongseong Hospital closed due to
an unknown contagious disease!

57:39.873 --> 57:41.249
[man 1] Mr. Chae was right.

57:41.332 --> 57:44.377
He told me they took a truckful
of corpses from Ongseong Hospital

57:44.461 --> 57:45.503
and buried them in a pit!

57:45.587 --> 57:48.339
- [man 2] Oh my, truckfuls of corpses?!
- Breaking news!

57:48.423 --> 57:52.010
ONGSEONG HOSPITAL CLOSED INDEFINITELY
POSSIBLY DUE TO CONTAGIOUS DISEASE

57:52.093 --> 57:53.761
[dramatic music playing]

57:57.098 --> 57:58.141
[solder 1] Let's go!

57:58.975 --> 58:00.185
Hurry up! Quickly!

58:01.144 --> 58:02.437
Faster! Go, hurry!

58:02.520 --> 58:04.856
Bring it over here!
I told you to hurry up!

58:05.565 --> 58:07.400
Let's go! Move! Move!

58:08.735 --> 58:10.111
CLOSED

58:23.583 --> 58:25.835
[woman] Did something happen yesterday?

58:25.919 --> 58:29.631
- [confused muttering]
- [man 3] They closed off the road!

58:31.257 --> 58:32.300
What are you saying?

58:32.383 --> 58:34.260
The Japanese military
barricaded the hospital?

58:34.344 --> 58:36.471
Um, yes.
No one can go inside the hospital.

58:36.554 --> 58:38.848
Anyone who was still inside
isn't able to leave.

58:38.932 --> 58:40.975
The Japanese soldiers
had machine guns and rifles,

58:41.059 --> 58:42.435
and it looked scary to me.

58:43.186 --> 58:44.812
[Mr. Gu] Have you heard from the sleuths?

58:45.647 --> 58:47.607
They might still be stuck in the hospital.

58:47.690 --> 58:48.525
[Mr. Gu sighs]

58:54.781 --> 58:56.866
Master Jang, wait. Where are you going?

58:56.950 --> 58:58.409
Hey, do I need to go too?

58:59.285 --> 59:00.662
Don't just stand there, go!

59:00.745 --> 59:02.747
Yes, I know. I was about to go with him.

59:09.420 --> 59:10.255
[door opens]

59:11.089 --> 59:12.215
[door closes]

59:15.677 --> 59:17.303
[suspenseful music playing]

59:18.096 --> 59:19.305
So I double-checked.

59:19.389 --> 59:22.267
Dr. Takahashi is unfortunately
out of the office today.

59:22.850 --> 59:24.060
What can I do for you?

59:32.318 --> 59:34.487
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

59:36.447 --> 59:38.074
Where's the person who gave this to you?

59:38.157 --> 59:40.243
Still trapped inside of the hospital.

59:41.536 --> 59:43.288
I managed to escape

59:43.371 --> 59:46.207
right before the soldiers got there
and barricaded it.

59:47.292 --> 59:48.293
It's shut for good.

59:50.044 --> 59:52.046
And those still trapped inside,
will they be safe?

59:54.215 --> 59:55.174
I don't know, sir.

59:55.258 --> 59:59.012
Is it true that there's a disease
spreading inside of that hospital?

01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:01.681
I don't know. I'm sorry.

01:00:01.764 --> 01:00:03.850
Why won't you give me a direct answer?

01:00:04.934 --> 01:00:07.186
Tell me what the hell is going on
inside of that hospital!

01:00:07.270 --> 01:00:09.147
I'm sorry, I don't know either!

01:00:14.110 --> 01:00:16.279
So many people died last night.

01:00:16.362 --> 01:00:17.697
[breathing shakily]

01:00:18.323 --> 01:00:20.617
So many innocent people died there!

01:00:23.161 --> 01:00:25.955
There were so many bodies.
Too many to even count.

01:00:26.623 --> 01:00:27.957
I don't know why.

01:00:28.625 --> 01:00:30.627
There's no way to find out either.

01:00:33.212 --> 01:00:34.297
Why was it you?

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:37.884
Why were you the one
who delivered this note to us?

01:00:38.384 --> 01:00:40.803
- Go ahead, tell me.
- [nurse breathing shakily]

01:00:42.972 --> 01:00:44.390
[suspenseful music playing]

01:00:54.817 --> 01:00:58.154
Some horrible things are happening
in that hospital right now.

01:00:58.905 --> 01:01:02.075
So many people have died in there.
We don't know why.

01:01:02.158 --> 01:01:03.117
[dramatic music playing]

01:01:03.201 --> 01:01:07.205
My comrades tried over and over
to find out what's going on, but…

01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:11.167
nobody ever comes back alive.

01:01:14.504 --> 01:01:15.672
Whoever is in there

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:17.965
won't make it back out.

01:01:21.844 --> 01:01:24.806
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

01:01:38.986 --> 01:01:41.030
[creature snarling]

01:01:43.533 --> 01:01:46.411
[creature roaring]

01:01:52.458 --> 01:01:54.502
- Mr. Gu.
- Yes, what is it, sir?

01:01:55.128 --> 01:01:57.672
It seems as if I'll have to go inside.

01:01:57.755 --> 01:01:59.006
Go inside? Huh?

01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:01.843
- Inside the hospital.
- You can't, sir!

01:02:01.926 --> 01:02:03.428
- Think about it!
- You can't!

01:02:05.346 --> 01:02:06.597
Get my things ready.

01:02:07.306 --> 01:02:09.016
It's happening. I'm going inside.

01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:11.936
["Forever" by SUHO playing]

01:02:15.398 --> 01:02:16.482
♪ Stuck in my head ♪

01:02:16.566 --> 01:02:18.484
♪ I've been searchin' for the reason ♪

01:02:21.446 --> 01:02:23.156
♪ Nameless longing ♪

01:02:23.239 --> 01:02:25.742
♪ I've been waitin' for you for so long ♪

01:02:25.825 --> 01:02:27.243
♪ For so long ♪

01:02:27.326 --> 01:02:31.205
♪ But got no direction
No matter, I wanna reach you ♪

01:02:32.206 --> 01:02:35.209
♪ Another way you runnin'
Goin' on and on ♪

01:02:35.293 --> 01:02:37.086
♪ But need a way to get to you ♪

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:41.257
♪ You ♪

01:02:41.966 --> 01:02:44.552
♪ You know, I'm so stuck with you ♪

01:02:44.635 --> 01:02:45.678
♪ No ♪

01:02:45.762 --> 01:02:47.388
♪ You ♪

01:02:48.014 --> 01:02:50.308
♪ Baby, I don't care at all ♪

01:02:50.808 --> 01:02:53.686
♪ You'll never know what I could do ♪

01:02:53.770 --> 01:02:56.522
♪ You'll never know
What we could have been ♪

01:02:56.606 --> 01:02:58.316
♪ For you, no, oh, oh, oh, oh ♪

01:02:58.399 --> 01:02:59.233
♪ Oh-oh-oh ♪

01:02:59.317 --> 01:03:01.068
♪ Do you know? ♪

01:03:01.569 --> 01:03:02.653
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:03:02.737 --> 01:03:04.489
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

01:03:04.572 --> 01:03:05.406
♪ Oh-oh-oh ♪

01:03:05.490 --> 01:03:07.325
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

01:03:07.408 --> 01:03:08.326
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:03:08.409 --> 01:03:10.036
♪ All the way I found you here ♪

01:03:10.536 --> 01:03:11.412
♪ Oh-oh-oh ♪

01:03:11.496 --> 01:03:13.456
♪ Oh, I'll be right back for you ♪

01:03:13.539 --> 01:03:14.582
♪ Oh, no ♪

01:03:18.544 --> 01:03:21.714
♪ Chasing the lights
Even don't know where I'm going ♪

01:03:24.300 --> 01:03:26.177
♪ Losing my sight ♪

01:03:26.260 --> 01:03:28.763
♪ Hope you know
That what I'm looking for ♪

01:03:28.846 --> 01:03:30.264
♪ Looking for ♪

01:03:30.348 --> 01:03:34.143
